From 2b96dbc4c94c0f99e75b3289b230241261025c25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ren=C3=A9=20Rebe?= <rene@exactco.de>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:49:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] powerpc: Restore PowerPC 601 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bring back the PowerPC 601 removed in v5.10 by f0ed73f3fa2c ("powerpc:
Remove PowerPC 601"), 8b14e1dff067 ("powerpc: Remove support for PowerPC
601"), e42a64002a50 ("powerpc: Remove CONFIG_PPC601_SYNC_FIX"),
d2a5cd83ee98 ("powerpc: Drop SYNC_601() ISYNC_601() and SYNC()"),
a4c5a3554229 ("powerpc: Remove __USE_RTC()") and follow ups, for the NuBus
Power Macintosh (PDM) and 601 PReP machines.

As before, a 601 kernel is a separate, uniprocessor build:

 - CONFIG_PPC_BOOK3S_601 with the 601 cpu_spec, excluding the 603 TLB
   and the other book3s/32 cpu_specs
 - 601 unified BATs at the IBAT SPRs, 8M maximum, valid bit in the lower
   BAT: initial 24M mapping, setbat, btext display BAT, ptdump, no
   strict RWX BAT updates, 16M initial memblock limit
 - the RTC instead of the timebase: get_tb()/mftb() return the RTC in
   nanoseconds and the decrementer counts nanoseconds, so the generic
   time code and the vDSO work at a 1 GHz "timebase"
 - no MSR[RI], no branch trace block step, TEA machine check without
   SRR1 bits, no KUEP (no segment N bit), no hibernation (no DBATs)
 - CONFIG_PPC601_SYNC_FIX sync/isync around MSR changes and rfi
 - bootwrapper udelay spin loop, no psurge SMP
 - a link time check that the kernel fits the initial 24 MB mapping, and
   a flat device tree beyond it is moved behind the kernel in real mode,
   as early_init_devtree() reads it through that mapping

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
